<file path="README.md">
  1: # Scripts
  2: 
  3: All scripts run from `server/` with `doppler run -- npx tsx src/scripts/<script>.ts`.
  4: 
  5: ## Core (production)
  6: 
  7: | Script | Purpose |
  8: |--------|---------|
  9: | `continuous-batch-scraper.ts` | Long-running DB-driven scraper. 4-tier term selection + 426-term fallback pool. |
 10: | `enqueue-batch.ts` | Config-driven CLI: `npx tsx src/scripts/enqueue-batch.ts <batchType>`. See `config/batch-configs.ts` for 17 batch types. |
 11: | `queue-results.ts` | Queue status + recent completed/failed jobs. `npm run queue:status` or `--limit N`. |
 12: | `worker.ts` | BullMQ worker process for scraper queue jobs. |
 13: 
 14: ## Config
 15: 
 16: | File | Purpose |
 17: |------|---------|
 18: | `config/batch-configs.ts` | 17 named batch types (LLC, trust, corporation, etc.) with priority tiers (-100 to 2). Includes `HIGH_RESULT_TERM_SPLITS` for high-volume terms. |
 19: 
 20: ## Enqueue
 21: 
 22: | Script | Purpose |
 23: |--------|---------|
 24: | `enqueue-terms.ts` | Enqueue arbitrary terms from CLI args. |
 25: | `enqueue-prefix-expansions.ts` | Generate and enqueue prefix-expanded terms (e.g., `Court` -> `Courta`..`Courtz`). |
 26: | `enqueue-uncommon-names.ts` | Enqueue curated uncommon name terms. |
 27: | `enqueue-test-batch-20.ts` | Enqueue a small 20-term test batch. |
 28: | `enqueue-08-08-search.ts` | One-shot: 193 terms from `docs/08-08-2026-search.md` with monitor. |
 29: 
 30: ## Backfill
 31: 
 32: | Script | Purpose |
 33: |--------|---------|
 34: | `backfill-2025.ts` | Primary 2025 backfill using DB-driven term selection. |
 35: | `backfill-2025-proven.ts` | Backfill using only proven high-yield terms from analytics. |
 36: | `backfill-2025-unsearched.ts` | Backfill using terms not yet searched in 2025. |
 37: | `backfill-2025-novel.ts` | Backfill using novel/experimental term patterns. |
 38: | `run-until-target.ts` | Run scraper until a target property count is reached. |
 39: 
 40: ## Analysis
 41: 
 42: | Script | Purpose |
 43: |--------|---------|
 44: | `analyze-failed-jobs.ts` | Categorize and report on failed scrape jobs. |
 45: | `analyze-search-terms.ts` | Analyze search term effectiveness from analytics data. |
 46: | `generate-search-terms.ts` | Generate candidate search terms for enqueue. |
 47: | `generate-next-200-terms.ts` | Generate the next 200 unsearched terms. |
 48: | `generate-valid-5char-terms.ts` | Generate valid 5-char terms from dictionary, filtering known failures. |
 49: | `check-unsearched-terms.ts` | Find inventory terms (593 total) not yet searched for current year. Uses batched EXISTS queries. |
 50: 
 51: ## Queue Management
 52: 
 53: | Script | Purpose |
 54: |--------|---------|
 55: | `check-queue-status.ts` | Quick queue size check (waiting/active/completed/failed). |
 56: | `clear-all-jobs.ts` | Clear all jobs from the queue. |
 57: | `auto-requeue-on-401.ts` | Watch for 401 failures and auto-requeue with fresh tokens. |
 58: | `queue-entity-searches.ts` | Enqueue entity-type search terms (Trust, LLC, Corp, etc.). |
 59: | `queue-entity-searches-fresh.ts` | Same as above with fresh token refresh first. |
 60: 
 61: ## Token & Debug
 62: 
 63: | Script | Purpose |
 64: |--------|---------|
